-- A record field's TYPICALLY default is worked out where its DECLARE is written,
-- like a rule's input: a name in it means what that name means in the section
-- the record is declared in, not what it means at the top of the file
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7, §4.3, silent review S2). It was looked up
-- from the top of the file, so a section's own `phi` was passed over for the
-- file's, with no error.

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 1000

§ `Rates`
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    phi MEANS 8

    DECLARE Config HAS
      timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi TIMES 2)
      retries IS A NUMBER

    -- the same default, on a rule's input, in the same section
    GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
          k IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi TIMES 2)
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    f MEANS n PLUS k

#ASSERT (Config WITH retries IS 1)'s timeout EQUALS 16
#ASSERT (f WITH n IS 0) EQUALS 16
